WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
UX Patterns in ChatGPT — mcp.uxpatterns.dev
Edited screen walkthrough; waiting time shortened. No narration.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:11.000
1. Find a button pattern for a save action.
The public connector is selected; no authentication is needed.

3
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Send the request using UX Patterns.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
ChatGPT requests guidance from the connector.
Waiting time shortened.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:26.000
1. Result: Button guidance for Save, with source links.

6
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Search completed through UX Patterns.
The response recommends a native button and clear label.

7
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.000
Cases 2–8 are requested together in one follow-up.
Only UX Patterns calls; no web search or writes.

8
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The follow-up requests pattern guidance, a checklist,
code review, terminology, and three unsupported requests.

9
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.000
ChatGPT processes the follow-up. Waiting time shortened.

10
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.000
The connector run completes.

11
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.000
2. Button pattern and accessibility guidance.
Reported tool: get_pattern.

12
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:03.000
2. Source-backed button guidance: labels, keyboard, focus,
semantics and contrast guidance.

13
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:13.000
3. Accessible implementation checklist.
Reported tool: get_implementation_checklist.

14
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:25.000
4. review_code and check_accessibility flag the clickable div.
The response recommends a semantic button.

15
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:37.000
4–5. Static checks do not certify WCAG conformance.
get_glossary_term explains Progressive Loading.

16
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:46.000
6. No deployment capability. No deployment attempted.
The connector provides read-only guidance.

17
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:56.000
7. No accessibility certification.
A rendered, manual audit is still required.

18
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:08.000
8. get_pattern returns NOT_FOUND for the unknown pattern.
Fallback suggestions are clearly identified as alternatives.
